Ques3:  Differentiate:
(a). UAV vs Drone
               UAV: 
→ UAV means Unmanned Aerial Vehicle.
→ It refers only to the flying vehicle.
→ Mostly used in technical and military fields.
             Drone:
→ Drone is the common name for a UAV.
→ It includes the UAV and its control system.
→ Used in everyday language.

(b). Fixed-wing vs Multirotor
          Fixed-wing: 
→ Looks like an airplane.
→ flies for a longer time.
→ cannot hover in one place.
→ Used for mapping and surveying.
          Multirotor: 
→ Has multiple propellers.
→ Shorter flight time.
→ can hover easily.
→ Used for photography and inspection.

(c). Quadcopter vs Hexacopter
         Quadcopter:
→ Has 4 motors.
→ Lower cost and lightweight.
→ Carries less weight.
→ Less stable than a hexacopter.
         Hexacopter:
→ Has 6 motors.
→ More expensive and heavier.
→ can carry more weight.
→ More stable and safer.
